rds": []}], "intertext": "The fragment VAT 10217 comes from near the left edge, with text preserved on both sides. Because of the damaged state of Assyrian MS x little of it can be translated. Nowhere is comparison with the Standard Babylonian version fruitful. The obverse holds the remains of Gilgameš’s telling of one of his nightmares. He had seen a figure of exceptional height and woken frightened. The reverse yields slightly more text but in terms of plot much of it is unintelligible. The only certainties are that there is a message to turn back home, presumably articulated in another of Gilgameš’s dreams, and that Enkidu then explains the dream, no doubt revealing it as favourable (adapted from @bib{RN117@361})."}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] … […]"}, {"number": "2'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [...] ... [...]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o", "i"], "number": "2'", "atf": "[...] x bu me [...]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] … […]"}, {"number": "3'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [...] ... [...]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o", "i"], "number": "3'", "atf": "[...] x x x x x li# x [...]\n$ single ruling", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] … […]"}, {"number": "4'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [...] ... [...]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o", "i"], "number": "4'", "atf": "[...] x-ki-ma qa-a-x it-ta-[...]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] … and … […]"}, {"number": "5'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [...] ... | ina ammā